---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"library\", \"diff\"])"
---
Compare a library profile with a slot of the pad, live (needs control channel v1.4). It shows what `library apply` writes: the label, the state, and each button that changes. It reads only. Exit 0: no change; exit 1: `apply` writes

Usage: gamepadii library diff [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>
          The name of the profile, any case

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --slot <N>
          The slot: 2 to 6 [default: the enabled slot with the label of the profile]

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
